+## Cross-repository Issues (research-only prototype)
+
+All four Issue tools (issue_read, issue_list, issue_update and
+issue_add_comment) accept an optional repo field with a GitHub
+owner/name identity. An explicit target avoids the need to open a
+local checkout or GitHub web UI. Omitting repo preserves original
+cwd-based repository inference.
+
+Examples:
+- issue_list: {"repo":"acme/server","labels":["bug"]}
+- issue_read: {"repo":"acme/server","number":42}
+- issue_update: {"repo":"acme/server","number":42,"title":"Clarify timeout"}
+- issue_add_comment: {"repo":"acme/server","number":42,"body":"Verified in staging"}
+
+Mutations still require approval with the full repository identity
+shown in the preview. Malformed targets fail closed instead of
+falling back to cwd. This is a source-native research proposal,
+not a feature shipped by upstream and not a measured user benefit.
 
